# .trivyignore - Trivy Security Scanner Ignore File
# Use this file to ignore specific vulnerabilities that are false positives
# or have been reviewed and accepted as risks

# Format:
# CVE-YYYY-NNNN
# or with expiry date:
# CVE-YYYY-NNNN exp:2025-12-31

# Example ignores (uncomment and modify as needed):
# CVE-2023-12345  # False positive in development dependency
# CVE-2023-67890 exp:2025-03-01  # Accepted risk, review by March 2025

# Ignore test files and documentation
**/test/**
**/tests/**
**/*.test.js
**/*.spec.js
**/node_modules/**
**/.git/**
**/documentation/**
**/*.md

# Ignore specific file patterns that may trigger false positives
**/*.min.js
**/*.map
**/vendor/**